ulated that there is  still so so much that has to happen in  the story given all the foreshadowing  that we've gotten over all these years  and anyways this chapter actually closes  a lot of open plot points while opening  up a bunch of others at the same time  and actually want to start with the  ending of this chapter where we finally  finally see admiral green bull ryoku  taking action and making his way to wano  by flying through the air using what  looks like a flower as a propeller this  is a huge deal in a number of ways first  of all it guarantees that we're about to  see his face revealed for the very first  time  we're also about to have one of the  strongest characters in the story make  an appearance in wano the flower on his  back seems to strongly suggest that many  of the plant-based theories surrounding  green bowl were actually true for some  reason it has been speculated for a long  long time now that green bowl might have  a plant-based ability based on both the  colored green and the fact that he  doesn't eat which might have hinted at  that the admiral is using photosynthesis  to actually you know get his nutrition  and stuff and if that is actually true  and this last panel really seems to  suggest that that could mean that green  bowl is a plant logia fruit user someone  whose body is literally made out of  plants which is why he could actually  survive on sunlight alone and girls if i  remember correctly even more  interestingly however is the question  why he's going to hano on his own in the  first place against the will and the  command of akainu who by the way doesn't  seem to have very good control over his  admirals and we're being completely  honest here they all just kind of do  whatever they like now i really don't  know about you but somehow green ball  doesn't give off the vibe that he's  trying to pick a fight with luffy and  cohere if you have to follow my gut  feeling on this i want to say that he  seems much more excited about the fact  that wano has been freed from kaido's  rule that would of course wonderfully  tie in with the idea that both fujitora  and green ball are actually citizens of  wano former samurai that were defeated  by kaido and joined up with the marines  not only would that explain fujitora's  crazy japanese theme and why he blinded  himself seeing all the horrors of mono  but also how the marines were able to  find two such powerful fighters in the  first place lying around guano is pretty  much one of the only places on the  entire grand line where ridiculously  powerful people just randomly live there  was also a lot of speculation that green  bull might be either one of the former  daimyo or even zorro's father either of  which let's be real would be absolutely  epic if true the fact that greenball is  still on his way right now also gives me  a bit of hope that we're not actually  gonna leave wano right next chapter but  that we still have a bit more time to  actually say goodbye to the country of  the samurai and just enjoy the end of  the fight super excited for that and i  can't wait to make a video on green ball  suit as well honestly the next thing we  have to talk about of course is the  gorosei tasking zp0 with capturing and  delivering rob into them now this would  be concerning enough by itself but what  really is worrying me is that robin is  suspiciously absent in this chapter like  completely she's nowhere to be seen  seven days after this specific order has  been given the last time we saw her if i  remember correctly was when yamato  introduced herself to the crew now  however she's neither with frankie and  usopp nor at luffy's sickbed nor in the  pretty wild bathhouse scene that oda  kindly enough threw in this chapter for  us as well we'll we'll get to that in a  while and so the fact that robin is  pretty much the only straw hat missing  in a chapter where her kidnapping has  been ordered by the rulers of the  goddamn world is pretty disturbing t